      "raw": "<p>I&#39;m not sure when oversized villain cards will be back. &nbsp; The preorder page for Villains of the Multiverse does state this:</p><p>\n> </p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 19px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto;\">Additional Bonus!</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 19px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; background-color: rgb(204, 213, 216);\">&nbsp;Every preorder of&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 19px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto;\">Villains of the Multiverse</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 19px; -webkit-text-size-adjust: auto; background-color: rgb(204, 213, 216);\">&nbsp;comes with three art prints and 7 promo cards. More info to come on all of those promos!</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">\n</span></p><p>So while it will net you the promo hero cards you will still have to separately preorder Chokepoint and Celestrial Tribunal as well if you want those. &nbsp;</p>",
